      "question": "I want to know if Transformer 1 at MAIN is running hot compared with its load. Over the available data window, summarize top-oil temperature (oti), its alarm and trip readings (oti_a, oti_t), and the three phase currents (il1, il2, il3) with neutral current (inut), giving min, max and mean for each. Then tell me whether the highest oti reading happened at the same timestamp as the highest total phase current. Flag any phase whose mean current differs from the other phases' average by more than 10%. If oti has no data, use ati for context and say that the thermal correlation can't be confirmed.",
      "answer": "**Transformer 1 (MAIN) has data for 5 daily readings, 2024-01-15 to 2024-01-19.**\n\n| Sensor | Min | Max | Mean |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| oti (°C) | 84 | 87 | 85.4 |\n| oti_a | 1 | 2 | 1.8 |\n| oti_t | 1 | 1 | 1.0 |\n| il1 (A) | 100 | 102 | 100.6 |\n| il2 (A) | 103 | 106 | 104.6 |\n| il3 (A) | 94 | 96 | 95.0 |\n| inut (A) | 5 | 6 | 5.2 |\n\noti has data, so I didn't need to fall back on ati. For context, ati was 77–79 °C (mean 78).\n\n**Does the oti peak line up with the current peak? Yes, partly.**\n- The highest oti was 87 °C on **2024-01-16**.\n- Total phase current (il1+il2+il3) was 300, 301, 299, 301 and 300 A over the five days. The highest, 301 A, happened twice: on **2024-01-16** and 2024-01-18. So the oti peak falls on one of the two tied current peaks.\n- oti goes up and down with total current across all five days: lowest on 01-17 (84 °C, 299 A) and highest on 01-16 and 01-18 (87 and 86 °C, 301 A). But the current only varies by about 0.7%, so this doesn't show much of a link.\n\n**Phase imbalance (each phase's mean compared with the average of the other two):**\n- il1: 100.6 vs 99.8 → +0.8%\n- il2: 104.6 vs 97.8 → +7.0%\n- il3: 95.0 vs 102.6 → −7.4%\n- **No phase is more than 10% off.** il2 runs highest and il3 lowest, but both are within the threshold. Neutral current is small and steady at 5–6 A.\n\n**Is it running hot for its load?**\n- Load is flat at about 100 A per phase, yet oti stays at 84–87 °C. I can't judge that against a rating because the data has no rated current.\n- Most of that heat looks like it comes from the surroundings. ati is already 77–79 °C, so the oil is only about 7–8 °C above ambient.\n- **The alarm and trip readings need checking.** oti_t reads 1 in every record and oti_a reads 1 or 2 (2 in four of the five records). If these are on/off flags, a trip was active the whole time and the alarm values aren't valid for a simple on/off signal. Someone should check what these readings mean and whether the protection is working properly.",
      "score": {
        "scorer": "llm_judge",
        "passed": false,
        "score": 0.8,
        "rationale": "The agent correctly retrieved stats for Transformer 1 at MAIN via iot.sensor_stats (min/max/mean for oti, oti_a, oti_t, il1, il2, il3, inut all match the tool output), pulled aligned history to compare the oti peak (2024-01-16, 87 °C) with the total-current peak (301 A on 01-16 and 01-18, tied), and computed the phase-imbalance check correctly (il2 +7.0%, il3 −7.4%, none exceeding 10%). The reported daily values are internally consistent with the stats (sums and means reconcile). However, the ag",
