          "suggestions": "The agent correctly retrieved stats for Transformer 1 at MAIN via iot.sensor_stats (min/max/mean for oti, oti_a, oti_t, il1, il2, il3, inut all match the tool output), pulled aligned history to compare the oti peak (2024-01-16, 87 °C) with the total-current peak (301 A on 01-16 and 01-18, tied), and computed the phase-imbalance check correctly (il2 +7.0%, il3 −7.4%, none exceeding 10%). The reported daily values are internally consistent with the stats (sums and means reconcile). However, the agent skipped the explicit iot.stream_extent and iot.installed_sensors calls that the expected behavior specifies to confirm the data window and available channels; it inferred these from sensor_stats output instead. Future runs should call stream_extent and installed_sensors first to explicitly verify the window and sensor availability before pulling stats and history. Optionally, fmsr.assess_load_profile could be used to support the 'running hot vs. load' judgment."
